precept TaxRateConfiguration

# A stateless data-only precept governing a tax rate configuration record for a
# single jurisdiction. Holds the headline rate plus optional surtax components,
# the effective window in which the configuration is active, and a derived
# combined rate the host application reads when computing tax on an invoice.
#
# Tax rates are administrative reference data — they are written by tax
# governance workflows in the host application. This precept focuses on the
# structural invariants every tax record must satisfy: rates are bounded
# between 0% and 100% (stored as decimal fractions, so 0.0875 == 8.75%), the
# effective window is well-formed, and only specific jurisdictions and tax
# categories are accepted.
#
# Compounding governs how the combined rate is derived:
#   Compounding == false (additive) — Combined = StateRate + LocalRate + SurchargeRate
#   Compounding == true (multiplicative) — apply each rate in sequence, so a
#     subtotal of 100 with State 5% then Local 2% yields 100*1.05*1.02 = 107.10
#     instead of 100*1.07 = 107.00. Host applications inspect the Compounding
#     flag and use whichever derivation matches the jurisdiction's tax law.

field Jurisdiction as string optional maxlength 50 editable
field TaxCategory as choice of string("Sales","VAT","GST","Excise","Use","Withholding") default "Sales" editable
field CurrencyCode as currency default 'USD' editable

# Rate components — each stored as a decimal fraction in [0, 1].
field StateRate as decimal default 0 nonnegative max 1 maxplaces 6 editable
field LocalRate as decimal default 0 nonnegative max 1 maxplaces 6 editable
field SurchargeRate as decimal default 0 nonnegative max 1 maxplaces 6 editable

# Additive combined rate — the natural reading when Compounding is false.
field CombinedRateAdditive as decimal nonnegative <- StateRate + LocalRate + SurchargeRate

field EffectiveFrom as date optional editable
field EffectiveTo as date optional editable

field Description as string optional maxlength 200 editable
field Compounding as boolean default false editable
field Active as boolean default true editable

rule EffectiveTo >= EffectiveFrom when EffectiveFrom is set and EffectiveTo is set because "Effective window end {EffectiveTo} cannot precede the start {EffectiveFrom}"
rule CombinedRateAdditive <= 1 because "Combined tax rate {CombinedRateAdditive} cannot exceed 100% — check the component rates"
